#
# Conformance case: teleology/outcome-specific-compensation (issue #1055 W1, Task 5).
#
# Two outcome branches of a realized plan recover by DIFFERENT compensation actions: the driver selects the compensation named on THE realized outcome branch (logic:selectedCompensation), not a generic schema-level undo — two plans, each realizing a different branch, select different compensations.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/outcome-specific-compensation/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
